@page "/docs/installation"
@layout Layout.DocsLayout

<PageTitle>Installation · blux-ui</PageTitle>
<div class="pg-prose">
    <p class="pg-eyebrow">Getting started</p>
    <h1>Installation</h1>
    <p class="pg-lead">Add the package, register the services, and load one stylesheet.</p>

    <h2>1. Add the package</h2>
    <CodeBlock Code="dotnet add package Blux.UI --prerelease" />

    <h2>2. Register the services</h2>
    <p>Call <code>AddBluxUi</code> in the server <code>Program.cs</code> and in the client one, with the same configuration. A shared method in the client project keeps them in sync.</p>
    <CodeBlock Title="Program.cs" Code="@ProgramCs" />

    <h2>3. Load the styles</h2>
    <p>Without Tailwind in your app, load the precompiled stylesheet and its reset:</p>
    <CodeBlock Title="App.razor" Code="@AppRazor" />
    <p>With Tailwind v4 in your app, each build copies the Blux theme to <code>obj/blux/blux.theme.css</code>. Import it after Tailwind:</p>
    <CodeBlock Title="app.css" Code="@AppCss" />
    <p>No Node needed: <code>&lt;BluxTailwind&gt;true&lt;/BluxTailwind&gt;</code> compiles that stylesheet at build time with the Tailwind standalone CLI. See the <a href="/docs/tailwind">Tailwind</a> guide.</p>

    <h2>4. Use the components</h2>
    <CodeBlock Title="_Imports.razor" Code="@("@using Blux.UI")" />
    <p>Remove Bootstrap from the Blazor template, or import it in a cascade layer: CSS outside layers overrides Tailwind's.</p>

    <h2>MAUI Blazor Hybrid apps</h2>
    <p>
        In a MAUI app the package and the stylesheets are the same, but there are no render modes and no server. Call <code>AddBluxUi</code>
        from <code>MauiProgram.cs</code> (after <code>AddMauiBlazorWebView</code>), link <code>_content/Blux.UI/blux.preflight.css</code> and
        <code>blux.css</code> from <code>wwwroot/index.html</code>, and add <code>HeadOutlet</code> as a root component so <code>BxHead</code> can
        write the theme and fonts into the head. The <a href="/docs/maui">MAUI and Blazor Hybrid</a> guide has the details and the status of each platform.
    </p>
</div>

@code {
    private const string ProgramCs = """
        builder.Services.AddBluxUi(options =>
        {
            options.Button.Slot("base", "font-semibold");
        });
        """;

    private const string AppRazor = """
        <head>
            <BxColorModeScript />
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["_content/Blux.UI/blux.preflight.css"]" />
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["_content/Blux.UI/blux.css"]" />
        </head>
        """;

    private const string AppCss = """
        @import "tailwindcss";
        @import "../obj/blux/blux.theme.css";
        """;
}
